# Line-ending policy (decide-substrate P2 K0-repair-3, 2026-07-02).
#
# `.fenel` sources are CONTENT-HASHED (the parse-cache keys, the compiled
# parser/resolver manifest hashes) — their checkout bytes must be identical on
# every machine (Windows autocrlf, linux CI, macOS). The parser + cache-key
# layer also LF-canonicalizes at read (defense in depth); this pins the bytes
# at the git layer so worktrees agree in the first place.
*.fenel text eol=lf

# The generated artifacts that embed content hashes — keep byte-stable too.
implementations/typescript/engine/src/generated/*.ts text eol=lf
.fenel.lock text eol=lf

# Same reason, for the generated JSON (signature-substrate slice 3jw, rider 1).
# `generate-signature-honesty-claims.ts --check` compares the committed artifact
# against a fresh recomputation, and the repository-identity manifest + field
# catalog are compared the same way — so a CRLF materialization of
# byte-identical content would read as DRIFT on a fresh Windows clone
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) or on CI. All three are already `i/lf w/lf`, so this
# pins the current state rather than renormalizing anything.
implementations/typescript/engine/src/generated/*.json text eol=lf

# M3b artifact-owned freshness hashes the complete covered source/config byte
# universe rather than only generated outputs. Keep every text row in those
# roots byte-identical to its Git blob on Windows, Linux, and macOS while
# leaving binary rows untouched.
fenel/** text=auto eol=lf
implementations/typescript/engine/src/** text=auto eol=lf
implementations/typescript/engine/scripts/** text=auto eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yaml text eol=lf
.github/**/*.json text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
package.json text eol=lf
bun.lock text eol=lf
tsconfig.base.json text eol=lf
implementations/typescript/engine/package.json text eol=lf
implementations/typescript/engine/tsconfig*.json text eol=lf

# Raw-byte performance evidence and the source-column analyzer are bound by
# recorded hashes; do not translate their bytes on a Windows checkout.
workstreams/development-performance/notes/2026-11-03-evidence/** -text
workstreams/development-performance/notes/2026-11-04-evidence/** -text
workstreams/development-performance/notes/2026-11-03-overnight/remaining-loaded-profile.mjs -text
workstreams/development-performance/notes/2026-11-03-overnight/remaining-loaded-profile-evidence.json -text
implementations/typescript/engine/src/authoring/test-support/literal-witness-eager-2026-11-03.ts.txt -text
